ix) The District Legal Services Authority, Kancheepuram District, is further directed to monitor the progress of the case before the Deputy Commissioner of Labour in E.C. No.174/13 so that necessary legal assistance to the impleaded applicants in E.C. No.174/13 are provided to them at all stages of the proceedings, till it reaches a logical conclusion;
x) C.C. No.121/2013 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No.II, shall proceed in accordance with law and the trial court shall dispose of C.C. No.121/2013 as expeditiously as possible as per seniority of the case.
The parties to the said lis are directed to co- operate with the trial court for the early completion of trial.
Further, taking into consideration the request as made by the learned counsel for the petitioners, their appearance before the trial court is dispensed with except for their appearance for the purpose of receiving the copy of the proceedings u/s 207 Cr.P.C., framing of charges, questioning under Section 313 Cr.P.C. and on the day on which judgment is to be pronounced.
However, if for any particular reason, the presence of the petitioners is necessary, the trial court, at its wisdom, shall direct their appearance on those days.
Accordingly, this criminal original petition is dismissed with the aforesaid observations and directions.
Consequently, connected miscellaneous petition is closed.

